<title>UK: Damaged wheat carrier moved into Sri Lankan port.</title>
<headline>Damaged wheat carrier moved into Sri Lankan port.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulk carrier Athena, damaged in an explosion off the Sri Lankan port of Trincomalee on May 29, has shifted anchorage to the inner harbour for security reasons, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said onThursday.</p>
<p>The Greek-registered vessel was carrying 52,000 tonnes of Argentine wheat for Trincomalee when it was hit by an underwater explosion.</p>
<p>An operation to bail water out of the engine room was progressing well and should be completed by June 20. There was no information regarding repairs. A surveyor was due Thursday to assess the damage.</p>
</text>
